    "name": "Side-bar-item",
    "description": "SideBar item — the navigation row. lg-squared inset around an md compressed label (heights 40/52/60; the inset absorbs the half-leading), a swappable leading icon in the md cap cell, ghost ladder at rest, accent when selected (fill + strong underline ink + accent glyph/label), and a thin subtle underline as the list separator — items stack with no gap, the borders are the rhythm. Collapsed: an icon-only square (width = height = inset×2 + cap) — the icon centres itself, because (height − glyph)/2 = inset − (glyph − cap)/2 is an identity of the optical system. Has Menu: a chevron trails when expanded; a small corner flag (bottom-right) marks the submenu when collapsed.\n\nGenerated from eds.side-bar-item v0.2.0 — edit the contract, not this component.",
